{"unit_id":"hansjone__netxops#readme-1","repo":"hansjone/netxops","commit":"fb94c8a6a077678655b226a0228a8f2729044965","type":"readme","lang":"en","text":"dsh-netxops README · Netx Ops for DeepSeek Harness：Network operations, topology and business monitoring tools for DeepSeek Harness Desktop and Web. Publish tools and their skills to Netx Ops, selected presets, or all presets; revoke them at any time.","source":"extracted","section":"Netx Ops for DeepSeek Harness"}
{"unit_id":"hansjone__netxops#readme-2","repo":"hansjone/netxops","commit":"fb94c8a6a077678655b226a0228a8f2729044965","type":"readme","lang":"en","text":"dsh-netxops README · Install：In Harness **Plugins → Add plugin**, enter `github:hansjone/netxops`, or the absolute path to a released `dsh-netxops-<version>.tgz`. A release tarball is recommended for a fixed, tested version and avoids downloading from GitHub during installation.\n\nFor the Web CLI:\n\n```sh\ndsh plugin --profile web add github:hansjone/netxops\ndsh web\n```","source":"extracted","section":"Install"}
{"unit_id":"hansjone__netxops#readme-3","repo":"hansjone/netxops","commit":"fb94c8a6a077678655b226a0228a8f2729044965","type":"readme","lang":"en","text":"dsh-netxops README · Install：Only Netx Ops is required. IM delivery and scheduling are optional, separate plugins. Users do not need Bun, Python, a local source checkout, or a build step; runtime JS and skills are included. Harness supplies its own internal packages and React.\n\nSee the [installation and troubleshooting guide](docs/INSTALL.md).","source":"extracted","section":"Install"}
{"unit_id":"hansjone__netxops#readme-4","repo":"hansjone/netxops","commit":"fb94c8a6a077678655b226a0228a8f2729044965","type":"readme","lang":"en","text":"dsh-netxops README · Configure：1. Open **Settings → Plugins → Netx Ops** and enter your Netx API URL and token.\n2. Choose each capability group's target presets. The default enables operations and business monitoring in Netx Ops only; topology and publication to all presets start disabled.\n3. After installation or upgrade, restart the relevant Desktop or Web Host once and select **Netx Ops** for a new session.","source":"extracted","section":"Configure"}
{"unit_id":"hansjone__netxops#readme-5","repo":"hansjone/netxops","commit":"fb94c8a6a077678655b226a0228a8f2729044965","type":"readme","lang":"en","text":"dsh-netxops README · Configure：Publication switches and preset selection save automatically. Connection fields, model language, alarm settings and manually entered knowledge-base paths use **Save / Discard**, shown when a draft changes. Choosing a knowledge-base directory through the picker saves that path automatically.","source":"extracted","section":"Configure"}
{"unit_id":"hansjone__netxops#readme-6","repo":"hansjone/netxops","commit":"fb94c8a6a077678655b226a0228a8f2729044965","type":"readme","lang":"en","text":"dsh-netxops README · Configure：The master publication switch removes all plugin-managed Netx tools and skills while retaining selections. Subsequent publication changes apply on the next model request without restarting. API access requires a reachable Netx service and token permissions matching the requested tools.","source":"extracted","section":"Configure"}
{"unit_id":"hansjone__netxops#readme-7","repo":"hansjone/netxops","commit":"fb94c8a6a077678655b226a0228a8f2729044965","type":"readme","lang":"en","text":"dsh-netxops README · Configure：Optional features include alarm delivery to a Harness session or IM, knowledge-base skills and local memory, and downloading this Host's persisted sessions as a ZIP. See [knowledge-base configuration](docs/KNOWLEDGE_BASE.md) and the [tool map](docs/TOOL_MAP.md).","source":"extracted","section":"Configure"}
{"unit_id":"hansjone__netxops#readme-8","repo":"hansjone/netxops","commit":"fb94c8a6a077678655b226a0228a8f2729044965","type":"readme","lang":"en","text":"dsh-netxops README · Development and release：```sh\npnpm install --frozen-lockfile --ignore-scripts\nbun run bundle\nbun run release:check\nbun run test:release\n\nDevelopment requires Node.js 22, pnpm 11.7 and Bun 1.3.13 or later. Building and package installation tests use only public development dependencies. Full Harness integration tests and type checking additionally need a local Harness runtime; see [maintainer instructions](docs/RELEASING.md).","source":"extracted","section":"Development and release"}
{"unit_id":"hansjone__netxops#readme-9","repo":"hansjone/netxops","commit":"fb94c8a6a077678655b226a0228a8f2729044965","type":"readme","lang":"en","text":"dsh-netxops README · Development and release：Release checks detect stale or missing bundles, undeclared runtime dependencies and invalid metadata. Tests install the actual npm tarball offline in an isolated profile. CI repeats the package checks on Windows, macOS and Linux.","source":"extracted","section":"Development and release"}
{"unit_id":"hansjone__netxops#readme-10","repo":"hansjone/netxops","commit":"fb94c8a6a077678655b226a0228a8f2729044965","type":"readme","lang":"en","text":"dsh-netxops README · Development and release：Group skills (ops / topology / biz-monitor) are published by netx over `/mcp` `resources` and cached under `$DSH_HOME/netxops-mcp-skills/`. This package does not ship skill files. Operator-subset KB pack skills remain local (see [Knowledge base](docs/KNOWLEDGE_BASE.md)).\n\nImplementation and UI validation details: [Chinese review](docs/PUBLICATION-REVIEW.zh.md).","source":"extracted","section":"Development and release"}
